<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>What changes if Democrats win a majority in Congress?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:524c1362aa8816da391203196574306a5faf618ca802d12121151eb4a8534d3d</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T16:29:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-what-changes-if-democrats-win-a-majority-in-congress" /><summary type="html">Americans head to the polls on Tuesday for the US midterm elections, which could flip the majority in one or both houses of Congress from the Republicans to the Democrats. What would a Democratic majority mean for the country's political landscape, and how might Democrats move to keep President Donald Trump in check?</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Nine dead in small plane crash near Trump's Florida home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0464ed0124497e3909c5cc7bbaddee2c48588586c6b1759785b85ea511191b5d</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:33:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-nine-dead-in-small-plane-crash-near-trump-s-florida-home" /><summary type="html">Nine people were killed Sunday when the Learjet they were travelling in plummeted into a neighbourhood in southern Florida, just miles from US President Donald Trump's resort home of Mar-a-Lago, officials said.</summary></entry><entry><title>Heading into the midterms, 'no US president in recent times has been as unpopular as Donald Trump'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b648e9eb8b451ebd456eb6b910cd95d1488a684d93b4026fbb61bf6500c9fe75</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:25:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/heading-into-the-midterms-no-us-president-in-recent-times-has-been-as-unpopular-as-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Richard Johnson, Senior Lecturer in US Politics at Queen Mary University of London. He says that "Donald Trump is damaged goods at this point in his presidency." With this uncompromising assessment, Johnson takes us through the political forces shaping the 2026 US midterm elections. Far from assuming that Trump's formidable campaigning instincts can once again mobilize Republican voters, Johnson questions whether the president's political influence has become a liability for the very party he once transformed. He points to a potentially significant realignment within the American electorate. Economic grievances, rising living costs, trade disputes and disillusionment with the war in Iran appear, in Johnson's reading, to be weakening important elements of the coalition that sustained Trump's return to power. Particularly consequential is the possibility that Latino voters, agricultural communities and sections of the MAGA electorate may be reconsidering their political loyalties or withdrawing from electoral participation altogether.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Will Gen Z enthusiasm help turn Michigan Senate blue?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3b9c6c6a9bfd86651c313d7dfa7e7236a514d4eeb04c36fdbf58f919a17936d</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:03:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-us-midterms-will-gen-z-enthusiasm-help-turn-michigan-senate-blue" /><summary type="html">Michigan’s Senate seat is a must-win for the Democratic Party as it seeks to take control of the upper house of Congress. There’s a surge of energy behind progressive candidate Abdul El-Sayed, especially among younger voters. But can Gen Z's enthusiasm translate into votes and help Democrats win a critical Senate seat?</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: North Carolina farmers hit hard by inflation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:637f5f7409e6c33ea9d5dd0ef842bbfe98bc86e36c8c5c932291560b423b122d</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T13:13:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261102-us-midterm-elections-north-carolina-farmers-hit-hard-by-inflation" /><summary type="html">On the eve of the midterm elections, US President Donald Trump's unpopularity is impacting Republicans across the board. Many states with seats once considered Republican strongholds are now on shaky ground. One of them is North Carolina, a rural state where one in five jobs is tied to agriculture.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Michigan Democrat's endorsement of Republican ruffles critical Senate race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcbf14c7b328fd57ddd9bfdb65efbe89ab12f35a69d735b66b7f1e7d7c979cf7</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:41:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-michigan-democrat-s-endorsement-of-republican-ruffles-critical-senate-race-1" /><summary type="html">A prominent Michigan Democrat endorsed Republican Mike Rogers on Sunday, giving President Donald Trump's Republicans an unexpected boost in a critical US Senate race two days before midterm elections that will decide control of Congress.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Michigan Democrat Haley Stevens defects from party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b81edf23bff15d4fb54858b914365babe58c5dd6a3b9fdfa8db93d82b689d92</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:52:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-us-midterms-michigan-democrat-haley-stevens-defects-from-party" /><summary type="html">Democrats sought on Monday, November 2, to contain a rift in Michigan's US Senate race after one of their own crossed party lines to endorse the Republican candidate, as both parties made final pitches before midterm elections that will decide control of Congress. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Could Senate candidate James Talarico turn Texas blue?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd7cb92758b0db2b843a783f76ed0c139f608e3d8c53f690e6d1710f8f0793c3</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T10:30:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-us-midterms-could-senate-candidate-james-talarico-turn-texas-blue" /><summary type="html">In Texas, a Democrat hopes to achieve a feat not seen in the state for 38 years: winning a seat in the US Senate. James Talarico, a young elected official who openly and proudly professes his Christian faith, is facing off against Ken Paxton, a controversial figure in the Republican Party. And his campaign is even winning over some of Donald Trump’s voters.</summary></entry><entry><title>In California, illegal border crossings plummet under Trump administration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9300df6bca512b26a71c121a224f929f6f923ab34b75dbae5404cd47b42aa9e5</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T09:36:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261102-in-california-illegal-border-crossings-plummet-under-trump-administration" /><summary type="html">It was one of US President Donald Trump's major campaign promises in 2024: putting an end to illegal crossings along the southern US border. Today, official data shows that promise has been kept: arrests for illegal crossings have plummeted by more than 93 percent since the peak of arrests under then-US President Joe Biden.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Michigan Democrat stuns party to back Republican candidate in critical Senate race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8781c59c85ce099035dd7ae5c37f8625e94a782c1e3ac4029af06bba0aa34980</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T08:20:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-michigan-democrat-stuns-party-back-republican-candidate-critical-senate-race" /><summary type="html">A high-profile Democratic defection shook Michigan's Senate race on the eve of US midterm elections as Representative Haley Stevens threw her support behind Republican Mike Rogers rather than backing the Democratic candidate, Abdul Al-Sayed, who beat her in the primary race. The move exposed divisions within the party as control of Congress hangs in the balance.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Michigan Democrat's endorsement of Republican ruffles critical Senate race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:651de6df87da2e695e4d5eaacd459083c1a97a302de5ae524ea8303165793e4d</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T07:55:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/michigan-democrat-s-endorsement-of-republican-ruffles-critical-senate-race" /><summary type="html">A prominent Michigan Democrat endorsed Republican Mike Rogers on Sunday, giving President Donald Trump's Republicans an unexpected boost in a critical US Senate race two days before midterm elections that will decide control of Congress. FRANCE 24's Caroline Baum brings us more with this report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms 2026: Georgians on the front lines of the people’s war against data centres</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf4519a0322d0a172dc839bad5ad045d8d4c213603015f4787af460052355c7b</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T06:11:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-midterms-2026-georgians-front-lines-people-war-against-data-centres--f7902fa87f3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-midterms-2026-georgians-front-lines-people-war-against-data-centres" /><summary type="html">Artificial intelligence emerged as a major issue on the 2026 US midterm campaign trail, with opposition to data centres drawing supporters across partisan divides united over ecological worries, increased utility bills and business interests outweighing citizen concerns. Georgia, the top US market for data centre construction, has been on the front line of the struggle.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Halloween weekend shootings across US leave at least six dead, dozens wounded</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79ec75ad256520e5111e5eac873516aa568ead7242625777cfa1c16e519cd4f7</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T00:49:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-halloween-weekend-shootings-across-us-leave-at-least-six-dead-dozens-wounded--acbd7ff7fa9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-halloween-weekend-shootings-across-us-leave-at-least-six-dead-dozens-wounded" /><summary type="html">A spate of shootings in nightlife districts and near university campuses across the United States over Halloween weekend left at least six people dead and dozens wounded, with Dallas recording the highest toll. Police were investigating multiple incidents in several states, while some suspects remained at large.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Nine killed as business jet crashes into South Florida neighbourhood</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2a435a6c18678d0e1c9cffc195946b6eb44c11717e3dac91280fe22d67bed4a</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T23:45:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261101-nine-killed-as-business-jet-crashes-into-south-florida-neighbourhood--8c4ca3ac05fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261101-nine-killed-as-business-jet-crashes-into-south-florida-neighbourhood" /><summary type="html">A business jet plunged into a South Florida neighbourhood on Sunday, killing all nine people aboard and exploding into a fireball near homes and a busy road. The pilot had reported icing, precipitation and severe turbulence before the Learjet entered a steep dive, according to air traffic control recordings.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Michigan 'betrayal’ &amp; midterm manoeuvres</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:414ef35cfb66f105ef4176fb36041cff7cb7eefee78b5147951edcdb47f874c2</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T19:37:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261101-michigan-betrayal-mid-term-manouvres--587c9df436b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261101-michigan-betrayal-mid-term-manouvres" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24's Gavin Lee assesses the last-minute campaign dramas and takes a US election overview on the "must-watch states" alongside Professor Donald Green, Professor of Political Science at Columbia University and co-author of the definitive book "Get Out the Vote", and foreign affairs analyst Laurie Dundon, who previously served in the US State Department during the Clinton administration.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Democrats face leftward surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bc638e5477a475af5641012e055105904822651625a7889543d9f34467931d0</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T13:56:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-democrats-face-leftward-surge--a5f145f073e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-democrats-face-leftward-surge" /><summary type="html">As Democrats seek to regain control of Congress, divisions within the party are emerging over its future direction. A new wave of progressive candidates is pushing to shift priorities further to the left, challenging corporate money in politics and calling for universal healthcare, climate action and an end to police violence. Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Affordability at heart of Michigan race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d731700caee8db24f95f3d16045bfef1440b45ac130f5314c0deab5c37945918</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:39:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-affordability-at-heart-of-michigan-race--ad6ada0d04e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-affordability-at-heart-of-michigan-race" /><summary type="html">For many voters, the cost of living is the single biggest issue. Our reporters Jessica Le Masurier and Sarah Andersen travelled to Michigan to meet voters, where, according to one NGO, around 40% of the population struggle to afford basic necessities.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump vs MAGA: Why his movement is splitting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:408a8c87f0c175769b7f4b068967fe690a887435b22fd79a57fe2b045bfe5b61</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T10:11:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261031-trump-vs-maga-why-his-movement-is-splitting--4267dc0a4776.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261031-trump-vs-maga-why-his-movement-is-splitting" /><summary type="html">As the 2026 midterm elections approach, divisions within the MAGA camp are becoming increasingly visible. From the war in Iran and rising fuel prices to the Epstein files, several of Trump’s decisions are fuelling divisions among his most loyal supporters.
 
Once united by a shared vision of America, MAGA now brings together factions that increasingly disagree over foreign policy, the economy and what “America First” should actually mean. Yet Trump remains the central figure holding this political coalition together – and he is fighting to keep it that way.
 
Why are some of the president’s longtime allies distancing themselves from him? Can MAGA remain united despite these disagreements? And can Trump still mobilise his base ahead of the midterms?
 
🔍 Our journalist Stella Elgersma breaks down the divisions within the MAGA movement and Donald Trump’s strategy to rally his supporters, once again.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Atmosphere of fear': Trump moves to curtail voting rights ahead of the midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:296e2e3b5ef7c62637b0429d69092dd10407f3180796d10cfd7c0a217d2c32db</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T09:40:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-united-states-atmosphere-of-fear-trump-moves-to-curtail-voting-rights-ahead-of-the-midterms--ef0cd17927a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-united-states-atmosphere-of-fear-trump-moves-to-curtail-voting-rights-ahead-of-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">Americans vote on November 3 in midterm elections that could see Republicans lose control of Congress, endangering US President Donald Trump's legislative agenda. Under the US Constitution, elections are organized by the respective states – but that has not halted US President Donald Trump from trying to wield his influence ahead of the vote.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro posts video, says he fled Brazil due to ‘persecution’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7cb0dc0ab6d2bdb30edcf2da4cd800a15f4abc33cfab1a38b629f267e9def5f</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T06:25:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-flavio-bolsonaro-posts-video-says-he-fled-brazil-due-to-persecution--3ad01377532f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-flavio-bolsonaro-posts-video-says-he-fled-brazil-due-to-persecution" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro posted a video message on social media late Friday to declare he had fled to the US because he was a victim of 'persecution'. Bolsonaro, who lost Sunday's election runoff to President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, gave no details of how he left the country.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump admin approves potential Patriot missiles sale to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c8c74aa0582b48f388b43b035f9577c4d16fcce8743f364ecbeccfb6d8b0511</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T23:19:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-trump-admin-approves-potential-patriot-missiles-sale-to-ukraine--23216ec77f01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-trump-admin-approves-potential-patriot-missiles-sale-to-ukraine" /><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>MAGA: Why Trump's movement is fracturing?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d5b54d382d016282720c68679b22b9a4ebcc6a72e35198a50ad03cd823d1d73</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T18:01:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-maga-why-trump-s-movement-is-fracturing--e5d6b934be9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-maga-why-trump-s-movement-is-fracturing" /><summary type="html">As the 2026 midterm elections approach, divisions within the MAGA camp are becoming increasingly visible. From the war in Iran and rising fuel prices to the Epstein files, several of Trump’s decisions are fuelling divisions among his most loyal supporters.
 
Once united by a shared vision of America, MAGA now brings together factions that increasingly disagree over foreign policy, the economy and what “America First” should actually mean. Yet Trump remains the central figure holding this political coalition together – and he is fighting to keep it that way.
 
Why are some of the president’s longtime allies distancing themselves from him? Can MAGA remain united despite these disagreements? And can Trump still mobilise his base ahead of the midterms?
 
🔍 Our journalist Stella Elgersma breaks down the divisions within the MAGA movement and Donald Trump’s strategy to rally his supporters, once again.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Deeply hurt': Convicted murderer Christa Pike speaks out after botched execution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebe61b7c17d5eff0e9802cd6b0e34c93666f751a6d1415ab304651d747a02b73</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T15:29:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-deeply-hurt-convicted-murderer-christa-pike-speaks-out-after-botched-execution--142643fa6707.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-deeply-hurt-convicted-murderer-christa-pike-speaks-out-after-botched-execution" /><summary type="html">Tennessee death row inmate Christa Pike said she remains in constant pain after surviving a botched lethal injection in September, in her first public statement since the failed execution. She expressed gratitude for those who saved her life while urging compassion for her victim's family.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>How will the women's vote shape the US midterms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88a4ab5c7266bac86f7ab98cc45f13fd513b39ccf18236eff2699550ef02c12c</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:52:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261030-how-will-the-women-s-vote-shape-the-us-midterms--b24f5ee96a41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261030-how-will-the-women-s-vote-shape-the-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">With the US midterms approaching, we examine the power of the women's vote in an election that will shape the balance of power in Washington during Donald Trump’s final two years in office. Annette Young talks to Annie Karni, congressional correspondent for The New York Times and Kelly Dittmar, Director of Research at the Centre for American Women and Politics.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Texas Republicans accused of changing electoral rules ahead of midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dfc4aad6897a55c2bd677acf464a2077e3815fd083ff8038c68ef0ea7a82f192</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:07:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261030-texas-republicans-accused-of-changing-electoral-rules-ahead-of-midterms--6f6bffa6894f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261030-texas-republicans-accused-of-changing-electoral-rules-ahead-of-midterms" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections approaching, Republicans in Texas are being accused of changing electoral rules in their favour. In Tarrant County, near Dallas, they've cut the number of election-day polling places by nearly 30 percent. The decision is being challenged in court and adds to last year's state-wide redistricting, a move designed to benefit Republicans. But the measures could also help galvanise the Democratic opposition. FRANCE 24's Pierrick Leurent reports, with Wassim Cornet.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>‘Scared of crossing the border’: The Arizona farmers who rely on Mexican workers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a16474ccfe98f90163d6038cc1a9c6df73bdc563fa21f1698ba37bd37e557770</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T12:28:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-scared-of-crossing-the-border-the-arizona-farmers-who-rely-on-mexican-workers--23b97d7329e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-scared-of-crossing-the-border-the-arizona-farmers-who-rely-on-mexican-workers" /><summary type="html">The vast produce farms of Yuma County, Arizona, rely heavily on foreign workers who cross the border every day from Mexico. John Boelts, a farmer and staunch supporter of US President Donald Trump, praises the administration’s strict border controls – though he says that competing Republican factions have complicated efforts to hire foreign labourers.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: With deep-red states now in play, could blue wave redraw America's political landscape?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5674b0f0d31f1e1aac7a17b23ed9977994bc1c248dc5435dcac28fd3cc0a426d</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T09:30:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-with-deep-red-states-now-in-play-could-blue-wave-redraw-america-s-political-landscape--e432c3d01e5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-with-deep-red-states-now-in-play-could-blue-wave-redraw-america-s-political-landscape" /><summary type="html">With the US approaching a potentially consequential midterm election, the political landscape appears to be shifting. Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Dr Richard Johnson, Senior Lecturer in US Politics &amp; Policy at Queen Mary University of London, who examines the prospect of a sweeping Democratic victory. He argues that the party could achieve gains of a magnitude not seen since Barack Obama's historic presidential election in 2008. Johnson sees a combination of Democratic enthusiasm, and growing support among independents, white college-educated voters and Latinos, and signs of defections from Donald Trump's fiercely loyal electoral coalition.</summary></entry><entry><title>Michigan's El-Sayed targeted by Republicans in midterms race: Will the religion card work?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:180e3d0b9217459f4b64516ef56ceb8867e70d7c6cb26e261d52a2a58dee85de</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T19:31:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261029-michigan-s-el-sayed-targeted-by-republicans-in-midterms-race-will-the-religion-card-work--09b7ffd28c6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261029-michigan-s-el-sayed-targeted-by-republicans-in-midterms-race-will-the-religion-card-work" /><summary type="html">What in the name of political free speech is off limits? Can you say whatever you want on the campaign trail, no matter how false or racist it is?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Lt. Gen. Ben Hodges accuses Hegseth of 'getting rid of people who may have the courage to push back'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5b3049c4c7f6270c39c2b6adec1acd44693e2b65f9bc8f825249fa29f3693ec</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T18:09:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lt-gen-ben-hodges-accuses-hegseth-of-getting-rid-of-people-who-may-have-the-courage-to-push-back--e4aa5af8da14.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lt-gen-ben-hodges-accuses-hegseth-of-getting-rid-of-people-who-may-have-the-courage-to-push-back" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye welcomes Lt. General (ret.) Ben Hodges, former commander of US Army Europe and NATO Allied Land Command. The dismissal of senior military officers without public explanation raises fundamental questions about institutional trust and the relationship between civilian authority and military leadership. For General Hodges, the reported firing of Lt. General Brett Sylvia reflects a potentially troubling pattern within the Pentagon under Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth. Equally striking is his criticism of the reluctance of retired senior commanders to speak publicly against policies they consider damaging. Hodges said he was "disappointed and surprised" by the limited public resistance among former four-star generals.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro’s great escape: Is this the beginning of the end for ‘Bolsonarism’?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:498bd8c375744efb788a890a694a404638b05c4b6ed4ca5a5df41622edd6287e</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T16:19:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261029-flavio-bolsonaro-s-great-escape-is-this-the-beginning-of-the-end-for-bolsonarism--f513ed731885.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261029-flavio-bolsonaro-s-great-escape-is-this-the-beginning-of-the-end-for-bolsonarism" /><summary type="html">The Brazilian election results had barely been announced before the defeated presidential candidate, Flavio Bolsonaro, packed his bags and fled with his family to the United States. The move may have dealt a serious blow to the already tarnished family brand, but does it spell the end for “Bolsonarism”?</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
